  "notes": "{巻|ま}き{込|こ}む is a compound verb meaning to roll/wrap something in, or to involve someone in a situation.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Formed from {巻|ま}く (to wind) + {込|こ}む (into)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{巻|ま}き{込|こ}む: to involve someone in ~\n- 〜に{巻|ま}き{込|こ}まれる: to get caught up in ~ (passive)\n- {周|まわ}りを{巻|ま}き{込|こ}む: to involve those around you\n- {事件|じけん}に{巻|ま}き{込|こ}まれる: to get caught up in an incident\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nThe passive form {巻|ま}き{込|こ}まれる is very common and often implies being involuntarily dragged into a situation, whether a conflict, accident, or trouble.",
